<section class="block-section do">
  <span class="section-tag">Do</span>
  <h2>Today's work: the conversation, the syllabus, and Classroom</h2>
  <p class="sub">Whole-class, teacher-led. Nothing here is graded.</p>
  <div class="callout activity">
    <div class="callout-title">Where we live, and what we owe it</div>
    <p>This is how the course starts. Back to the video, four questions, as a whole class, in this order:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>How do you feel after watching that?</li>
      <li>What does it imply for us, as humans on Earth?</li>
      <li>What role do we have in looking after the environment, and what responsibility comes with it?</li>
      <li>What do we want to commit to, as a class, for this course and for the place we live?</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The first question has no wrong answer and every answer gets heard. Out of the last one we build two things together on chart paper, in our own words. <strong>Our creed:</strong> what this class commits to, for the course and for the environment. <strong>Our norms:</strong> how we agree to work with each other so that the creed is actually possible.</p>
    <p>The chart goes on the wall and stays there for the year. It is meant to be in front of us, not filed somewhere and forgotten, and it can be added to when we decide it is missing something.</p>
    <p>It sits alongside <a href="/foundations/class-expectations/">Class Expectations</a>, which is the working agreement your teachers bring. The creed and the norms are the half the class writes. We come back to the creed at the end of Unit 4, when you have the climate science, and again in Unit 6, when you redesign a piece of Chennai.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="choice-board">
    <div class="choice">
      <div class="choice-letter">1</div>
      <div class="choice-title">Syllabus walkthrough</div>
      <div class="choice-detail">We read the course expectations together and you ask anything you want about how the year works. Bring up the parts that seem unfair or unclear now rather than in November.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="choice">
      <div class="choice-letter">2</div>
